Another advantage is the reduction in commuting time. Many employees used to (2) ___ hours travelling to and from the office every day. By working from home, they can use this time more effectively.
However, remote working also comes with challenges. For example, it can be difficult to (3) ___ in touch with colleagues and maintain strong communication. Without regular face-to-face interaction, misunderstandings may occur more frequently.
In addition, some people find it hard to (4) ___ focused when working from home. There may be distractions such as household tasks or family members that interrupt their work.
To solve these problems, it is important to create a suitable working environment. Setting clear boundaries and having a dedicated workspace can (5) ___ a big difference.
Employers also play an important role by providing the right tools and support. Regular meetings and clear instructions can help teams (6) ___ connected and work efficiently.
